### Bug Analysis

#### Bug Scenario Description
The images show a dropdown component used to select icons. The issue arises when the selected item is displayed as `[object Object]` in the title attribute of the button, instead of a meaningful string or icon. This happens because the `itemToString` function is being used to render the selected item, which returns an object instead of a string.

#### Root Cause
The root cause of the issue is the misuse of the `itemToString` function to render elements instead of strings. The `itemToString` function is intended to convert an item to a string for display purposes, such as in the title attribute. However, it is being used to render elements, leading to the `[object Object]` output.

### Bug Fix

To fix this issue, we need to introduce a new prop, `renderSelectedItem`, which will determine whether to use `itemToElement` or `itemToString` for rendering the selected item. This will allow the developer to choose the appropriate rendering method.

